 "upstream_note": "AP_HAL_ChibiOS I2CDevice ctor: on H7, a device asking <=100 kHz lowers the whole bus to HAL_I2C_F7_100_TIMINGR (default 0x30812E3E, an F7/54 MHz value) instead of the H7 one. At 32 MHz that default is 62.2..71.5 kHz and Sm-NON-compliant (RM SCLDEL). I2C1 is the external bus (HAL_I2C_INTERNAL_MASK 0), so external-bus probes/drivers that request 100 kHz (AP_BattMonitor_INA2xx.cpp, AP_BattMonitor_INA3221.cpp, AP_BattMonitor_LTC2946.cpp, AP_BattMonitor_SMBus.cpp, AP_DAC_MCP40D1x.cpp) can trigger this path; hwdef.dat therefore overrides HAL_I2C_F7_100_TIMINGR (and HAL_I2C_H7_100_TIMINGR for consistency) with 0x4080231E, Sm-compliant for tr <= 1000 ns. Once lowered, the bus stays in Standard mode (78..93 kHz worst case) for all devices including the DPS310."
}